\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y=2{X}_{1}+{X}_{2} & ∼N(2\\cdot 10+1\\cdot 9,{2}^{2}\\cdot 8+{1}^{2}\\cdot 6) \\\\  & ∼N(29,38).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, $Y∼N(29,38).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186158768 :answer-field/correct "answer-ee4dd5fe-046c-5b11-bdfc-b33ee3662cf6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4defb62d-3136-51cb-ab90-0028809c8e41" "answer-043bf8e6-79bb-59f9-a755-a8b7fa7e28d0" "answer-ee4dd5fe-046c-5b11-bdfc-b33ee3662cf6" "answer-c599d068-635a-5031-a923-8e71c22fd844"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4defb62d-3136-51cb-ab90-0028809c8e41" :answer/id #uuid "4defb62d-3136-51cb-ab90-0028809c8e41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "N(19,36)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-043bf8e6-79bb-59f9-a755-a8b7fa7e28d0" :answer/id #uuid "043bf8e6-79bb-59f9-a755-a8b7fa7e28d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "N(29,36)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee4dd5fe-046c-5b11-bdfc-b33ee3662cf6" :answer/id #uuid "ee4dd5fe-046c-5b11-bdfc-b33ee3662cf6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "N(29,38)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c599d068-635a-5031-a923-8e71c22fd844" :answer/id #uuid "c599d068-635a-5031-a923-8e71c22fd844" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "N(29,48)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-00d2e780-6ff9-5f4c-863c-7e7274f9ff9d" :question/id #uuid "00d2e780-6ff9-5f4c-863c-7e7274f9ff9d" :question/math-academy-id "q-109660" :question/problem "If ${X}_{1}∼N(11,2)$ and ${X}_{2}∼N(-5,5)$ are independent, then what is the distribution of $Y=-2{X}_{1}+4{X}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if ${X}_{1}$ and ${X}_{2}$ are independent random variables, where ${X}_{1}∼N({\\mu }_{1},{\\sigma }_{1}^{2})$ and ${X}_{2}∼N({\\mu }_{2},{\\sigma }_{2}^{2}),$ and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then \n\n$$\na{X}_{1}+b{X}_{2}∼N(a{\\mu }_{1}+b{\\mu }_{2},{a}^{2}{\\sigma }_{1}^{2}+{b}^{2}{\\sigma }_{2}^{2}).\n$$\n\nSince ${X}_{1}$ and ${X}_{2}$ are independent, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y=-2{X}_{1}+4{X}_{2} & ∼N((-2)\\cdot 11+4\\cdot (-5),{2}^{2}\\cdot 2+(-4)^{2}\\cdot 5) \\\\  & ∼N(-42,88).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Y∼N(-42,88).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a0f714e9-65d4-50bf-bf90-76a91cd08c3d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a0f714e9-65d4-50bf-bf90-76a91cd08c3d" :answer-field/id #uuid "a0f714e9-65d4-50bf-bf90-76a91cd08c3d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8e9e62e3-8e73-5033-b67b-e561a5697f1d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b569977d-b799-5f87-954a-2601cb3ad53e" "answer-26c8576a-dfe9-5631-b5a0-92c11c46960d" "answer-93adf0e3-725d-5898-af43-d6af2272415b" "answer-8e9e62e3-8e73-5033-b67b-e561a5697f1d" "answer-f857ac78-49a1-5068-bc80-c53da60c1b36"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b569977d-b799-5f87-954a-2601cb3ad53e" :answer/id #uuid "b569977d-b799-5f87-954a-2601cb3ad53e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "N(-2,72)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-26c8576a-dfe9-5631-b5a0-92c11c46960d" :answer/id #uuid "26c8576a-dfe9-5631-b5a0-92c11c46960d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "N(-2,88)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-93adf0e3-725d-5898-af43-d6af2272415b" :answer/id #uuid "93adf0e3-725d-5898-af43-d6af2272415b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "N(-42,72)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e9e62e3-8e73-5033-b67b-e561a5697f1d" :answer/id #uuid "8e9e62e3-8e73-5033-b67b-e561a5697f1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "N(-42,88)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f857ac78-49a1-5068-bc80-c53da60c1b36" :answer/id #uuid "f857ac78-49a1-5068-bc80-c53da60c1b36" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Not enough information to determine the answer" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "