rked-solution "Recall that if ${X}_{1}$ and ${X}_{2}$ are independent random variables, where ${X}_{1}∼N({\\mu }_{1},{\\sigma }_{1}^{2})$ and ${X}_{2}∼N({\\mu }_{2},{\\sigma }_{2}^{2})$, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then \n\n$$\na{X}_{1}+b{X}_{2}∼N(a{\\mu }_{1}+b{\\mu }_{2},{a}^{2}{\\sigma }_{1}^{2}+{b}^{2}{\\sigma }_{2}^{2}).\n$$\n\nSince ${X}_{1}$ and ${X}_{2}$ are independent, the distribution of $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y={X}_{1}-{X}_{2} & ∼N({\\mu }_{1}-{\\mu }_{2},{\\sigma }_{1}^{2}+{\\sigma }_{2}^{2}) \\\\  & ∼N(7-6,1+3) \\\\  & ∼N(1,4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Y$ is normally distributed with mean $\\mu =1$ and standard deviation $\\sigma =\\sqrt{4}=2.$ \n\nWe want to find $P(Y\\le 2.1).$ Thus, we convert $Y$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y\\le 2.1) & =P(Z\\le \\frac{2.1-1}{2}) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 0.55) \\\\  & =Φ(0.55)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the $z$-table, we see that\n\n$$\nΦ(0.55)≈0.7088.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(Y\\le 2.1)≈0.71.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b924a128-0c43-534a-9cba-90b2ae79b1e8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b924a128-0c43-534a-9cba-90b2ae79b1e8" :answer-field/id #uuid "b924a128-0c43-534a-9cba-90b2ae79b1e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5bed3c7f-0907-556f-84d5-c5847e9dc133" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6279118f-62e8-57d8-aefe-61881c9c418f" "answer-128b1dc4-16b3-5703-ac5a-3c02333f7673" "answer-257039f0-e2b5-59cd-9386-eac7326bfa18" "answer-5bed3c7f-0907-556f-84d5-c5847e9dc133" "answer-07a44495-46e9-54da-b5fe-e18a8be62591"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6279118f-62e8-57d8-aefe-61881c9c418f" :answer/id #uuid "6279118f-62e8-57d8-aefe-61881c9c418f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.64" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-128b1dc4-16b3-5703-ac5a-3c02333f7673" :answ