alidate]} {:db/id "answer-f8f9e9d1-5f7b-5120-b793-94523bcd4741" :answer/id #uuid "f8f9e9d1-5f7b-5120-b793-94523bcd4741" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "false" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-063d28fc-b64c-5b06-b4f0-daa8f90ffd36" :answer/id #uuid "063d28fc-b64c-5b06-b4f0-daa8f90ffd36" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "true" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c586014f-8b0b-5087-a740-57029ea9f0d3" :question/id #uuid "c586014f-8b0b-5087-a740-57029ea9f0d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-175666" :question/problem "$$\n{{5\\text{ is odd}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{-5\\in Z}_{⏟}}_{B}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $A$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $B$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $A∨B$ is {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(∧)$ and \"or\" $(∨)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A∧B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A∨B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $A$ is true, and $B$ is true. Therefore, the result is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{5\\text{ is odd}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{-5\\in Z}_{⏟}}_{B} & \\,\\,≡\\,\\text{true}∨\\text{true}≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c45c4194-12b2-5fe5-9c77-c08f6af56cd8" "answer-field-5c291b0e-f8c9-5939-a96e-0401075ed43c" "answer-field-a5302458-71fb-5afb-a950-a7024e57aebf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c45c4194-12b2-5fe5-9c77-c08f6af56cd8" :answer-field/id #uuid "c45c4194-12b2-5fe5-9c77-c08f6af56cd8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-374c1b92-a065-5d73-84bd-e768c04e2423" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2ea973ca-4c0d-5900-a76d-4213928289f8" "answer-374c1b92-a065-5d73-84bd-e768c04e2423"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/